# Cloudflare Pages custom headers. Not served itself; Pages parses it and applies
# these to every static asset response. Wrangler/Pages Functions do NOT get them,
# so keep this site static.
#
# Cross-origin isolation is not optional here. The kirikiri and Play! runtimes are
# built with pthreads, and a browser only offers SharedArrayBuffer - which those
# threads need - on a cross-origin-isolated page.
#
# require-corp blocks any cross-origin response without a Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy
# header of its own or a passing CORS check. The one cross-origin load is GoatCounter's
# count.js (index.html), loaded with crossorigin="anonymous" for exactly that reason.
#
# Cache-Control: Pages otherwise gives everything but the page itself a 4-hour
# max-age, so after a deploy a browser could pair the new index.html with
# yesterday's scripts (a new tab whose engine assets/library.js doesn't know
# yet), or a rebuilt engine's .js with its old .wasm. Revalidate everything
# instead: an unchanged file is a 304 with no body.
#
# Keep this one block: a second /* block replaces this one rather than adding
# to it, which silently drops the isolation headers.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Origin-Agent-Cluster: ?1
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
